-- THE COST, MEASURED AND NOT NETTED
-- The acceptance criterion for this wave is that no row the engine already
-- characterised stops being characterised. Checking that on the shape counters
-- (readable/thin/empty, strongN/splitN) is NOT good enough, and this wave is the
-- proof: on the aggregate counters Lee and Curtis appear not to move at all, because a
-- row that goes from unread to read-thin lands in thinN either way and never enters
-- the `characterised` figure. Checked directly on the row model's own `read` flag
-- instead, over every pid in the set, set-wise. That check finds 184 rows this wave
-- starts characterising and ONE it stops. The one is recorded in full rather than
-- netted against the 184, because a wave that reports only its wins is not measuring
-- itself.
--
-- Counted set-wise on the read flag: 184 rows start being characterised (177 thin, 5
-- mostly, 2 split; by key lands_preserve 103, broadband 73, lands_energy 8) and 1
-- stops (1 thin). The one loss is named in db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json under
-- readLossDisclosure.causes and is not netted against the gains. Utah: 4 gained, 0
-- lost.
--
-- · trent_kelly, lands_energy — a wall tripped, and it is admitted as a cost rather than
--   argued away — He holds three live lands_energy acts: H.J.Res. 131 at w100 PRIMARY,
--   on which he is recorded NOT VOTING, and two package secondaries (H.R. 26 w45, H.R. 1
--   w40) he voted yea on. His only primary act takes no side, so the primary wall has
--   nothing to count. Today three acts keep him under _RD_MIN_JUDGED and the engine
--   names the row thin. H.J.Res. 140's lands_energy secondary makes it four, which
--   crosses the floor onto the deepEnough branch, where the primary wall (primary < 1)
--   fires and the row goes unread. This is the rule-30 mechanism, not a surfaced
--   contradiction — all three of his recorded votes point the same way.
--   DECISION: Measured both ways before deciding. The lands_energy row gains EIGHT
--   characterised rows and costs this one, and it is the mirror row H.J.Res. 131's own
--   precedent requires — 131 files lands_preserve as its mirror secondary at w90 for the
--   same reason. Dropping it would have made this wave quieter and the record less true:
--   the resolution really does reopen 225,504 acres to mineral leasing, and a member who
--   voted for it has done that. The alternative cost is disclosed, not hidden, and it is
--   the reason the two gov_regulation secondaries — which gain ZERO and cost TWO by the
--   identical mechanism — were refused. The rule this wave applied is arithmetic, not
--   taste: a secondary is admitted when it gains more than it costs and refused when it
--   does not.
--
-- · jared_golden, lands_energy — a contradiction surfaced, not a wall tripped (rule 25)
--   — He keeps the row and keeps reading; the tier weakens from 15 clear issues to 14
--   and his split count rises. He voted NAY on H.J.Res. 131 (w100 PRIMARY yea_supports),
--   YEA on H.R. 26 and NAY on H.R. 1, and YEA on H.J.Res. 140. That is a genuinely mixed
--   record on the key and the engine now says so. Rule 25: a contradiction the record
--   contains should be surfaced, not smoothed. Not counted as a loss because the row is
--   still read.
--   DECISION: Nothing to weigh. Surfacing a real contradiction is the engine working.
--
-- · don_bacon, jared_golden — split rows gained — Two members gain a split row (bacon
--   6→7, golden 17→19). Both are members whose votes on the new measures run against
