-- · Sanders Amdt. 2126 to H.Con.Res. 14 (senate 119/1/184, 47-52 Rejected) — REFUSED AS
--   A MAPPING under rule 31, for the third consecutive wave. A budget-resolution
--   amendment establishing a pathway to consider a minimum-wage increase is not the wage
--   law; the operative verb is 'consider'. F1 refused it, F2 refused it, and it is
--   re-refused here rather than quietly omitted so that econ_workers' blocked-on state
--   cannot be read as an oversight.
-- · H.Con.Res. 14 (senate 119/1 Baldwin Amdt. 1693, reserve fund) — REFUSED under rule
--   31. Its opening clause is rule 31's first tell verbatim — 'To establish a
--   deficit-neutral reserve fund relating to…' — and it is the only Senate instrument
