  -- ── issue mappings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  -- Curated in db/vr-issue-seed.json with a rationale and an https primary source on every
  -- row — scripts/test-mapping-discipline.mjs requires both — and argued in db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json,
  -- which also records every refusal and the measurement behind it. ON CONFLICT
  -- (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING, so a re-emission cannot rewrite a rationale
  -- (runbook rule 21).

  -- S.J.Res. 7 (119th) — broadband yea_opposes w100 PRIMARY
  --   Federal wave F3. A Congressional Review Act joint resolution read from its engrossed
  --   text (govinfo BILLS-119sjres7es), which is one operative sentence, and from the
  --   disapproved rule's own Federal Register abstract. Filed on the SUBJECT axis ONLY.
  --   The gov_regulation process secondary that every live CRA in the record carries was
  --   drafted and then REFUSED on a measurement: it gains no characterised row and costs
  --   two (angus_king, lujan), by the rule-30 mechanism. public_schools, rural_ag and
  --   edu_college_cost were read and refused in writing. This is the FIRST broadband
  --   PRIMARY in the corpus in either chamber. See db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json for
  --   the argument, the near-unanimity and two-flank checks, and the refusals.
  --   Read and refused on this measure: gov_regulation, public_schools, rural_ag,
  --   edu_college_cost. The argument against each is in
  --   db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json.
  --   decisiveQuestion: 'On the Joint Resolution' on an S.J.Res. is the single entry in
  --   rule 12's PASSAGE_FORMS. Admitted on the form alone, so no decisiveWhy is written.
  --   The sibling roll on the same resolution — senate 119/1 roll 235, 'On the Motion to
  --   Proceed', 53-47, 2025-05-06 — is refused on question form under rule 8 and is
  --   recorded under declinedRollCalls.
  --   singleSubject: Read from the engrossed text (govinfo BILLS-119sjres7es), which is
  --   one operative sentence in full: 'That Congress disapproves the rule submitted by the
  --   Federal Communications Commission relating to ``Addressing the Homework Gap Through
  --   the E-Rate Program'' (89 Fed. Reg. 67303 (August 20, 2024)), and such rule shall
  --   have no force or effect.' There is no second subject, no reserve fund, no
  --   sense-of-the-Senate clause and no severable provision.
  --   notReserveFund: Correct. Rule 31's three textual tells — 'To establish a
  --   deficit-neutral reserve fund relating to…', 'To make sure the Senate can…', and an
  --   operative verb of 'consider' — are all absent. The operative verb is 'disapproves',
  --   and 5 U.S.C. 802 makes the effect operate by law on enactment.
  --   proceduralInversion: No. The question is the joint resolution itself, so
  --   yeaBlocksMeasure() does not fire and the ordinary direction holds: a yea advances
  --   the disapproval.
  --   nearUnanimity: No. 50-38 with 12 not voting. The losing side is 43.182% of the
  --   yea+nay pool, far above rule 11's one-tenth bar. Party totals from the document
  --   itself: R 50-0 yea, D 0-36 nay, I 0-2 nay.
  --   twoFlankNays: Checked (rule 5 / rule 23) and NO. All 38 nays argue the same thing —
  --   that the hotspot support should stand — so there is no second flank arguing the
  --   disapproval does not go far enough, and the headline key stands with no
  --   provision-level substitution. Read off the floor statements on the resolution rather
  --   than off the tally's party columns, deliberately: the two-flank test asks how many
  --   ARGUMENTS the losing side holds, and a party column cannot answer that question. The
  --   party split is recorded on the roll call itself, where it belongs, and is not
  --   reasoning here.
  --   enactedTier: Not law. Passed the Senate 2025-05-08 and went no further: govinfo
  --   holds is, es and pcs for this resolution and returns 302 for enr and eh, so there is
  --   no enrolled text and no House passage. Filed status 'passed_senate'.
  --   ruleStillInForce: Recorded, and it does not change the vote. The FCC itself
  --   rescinded the 2024 hotspot rules on reconsideration at 91 Fed. Reg. 2492
  --   (2026-01-21). The mapping is of the 2025 ACT, not of the rule's present status; a
  --   senator's recorded vote is not retroactively unmade by an agency doing the same
  --   thing later.
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_119_s_j_res_7, 'broadband', 100, true, 'yea_opposes',
      'The resolution''s whole operative text disapproves one named FCC rule, and that rule''s subject is household internet access. 89 Fed. Reg. 67303 states its own purpose: the Commission “takes steps to modernize the E-Rate program to meet the evolving needs of schools and libraries around the country by allowing for the distribution of Wi-Fi hotspots and services to students, school staff, and library patrons for off-premises use.” Off-premises use is the whole point — the rule pays for connectivity where the student is, not where the school is. broadband is ''Bring fast, affordable internet to rural and underserved communities'' and its keywords name ''internet access'', ''digital divide'', ''connectivity'', ''underserved'' and ''fcc''. A yea strikes the rule and withdraws the hotspot support, so the direction is yea_opposes. Primary at 100 because it is the resolution''s entire subject; the weight matches the primary weight of every CRA already in the record (H.J.Res. 25, 88, 89 and 131 all file their subject key at 100). This is the record''s first broadband PRIMARY in either chamber — the only other federal broadband row is a division-level secondary on H.R. 3684 at weight 65, which is exactly why the formal index reads the axis as incidental for 88 of 99 senators.',
      'https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/08/20/2024-18122/addressing-the-homework-gap-through-the-e-rate-program')
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;

  -- H.J.Res. 140 (119th) — lands_preserve yea_opposes w90 PRIMARY, lands_energy yea_supports w75
  --   Federal wave F3. A Congressional Review Act joint resolution read from its engrossed
  --   text (govinfo BILLS-119hjres140eh), which is one operative sentence, and from the
  --   disapproved order's own Federal Register abstract. Enacted as Public Law 119-85 on
  --   2026-04-27. Filed in the H.J.Res. 78 shape rather than the H.J.Res. 131 shape, and
  --   the discriminator is the one H.J.Res. 131's own rationale wrote down: what
  --   instrument does the disapproval act ON. 131 acted on a leasing programme decision,
  --   so lands_energy carried it; this one acts on a withdrawal order whose stated purpose
  --   is protection, so lands_preserve carries it. This is the FIRST lands_preserve
  --   PRIMARY a senator can reach. The gov_regulation process secondary that every live
  --   CRA in the record carries — including H.J.Res. 131, the only other BLM CRA — was
  --   drafted and then REFUSED on a measurement; see db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json.
  --   energy_production, water, climate_action, states_federal_power and rural_ag were
  --   read and refused in writing. See db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json.
  --   Read and refused on this measure: gov_regulation, energy_production, water,
  --   climate_action, states_federal_power, rural_ag. The argument against each is in
  --   db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f3.json.
  --   BOTH CHAMBERS: This is a HOUSE measure. Filing its Senate passage vote and
  --   withholding its House passage vote would create, inside the very wave that exists to
  --   close a chamber gap, the defect rule 30's second corollary names — a measure whose
  --   own chamber does not appear among its roll calls — and F2's chamberGapSweep flagged
  --   that pattern as almost always an ingest gap. So both halves of the measure's own
  --   record go in together. The wave's purpose is still the Senate side; the House roll
  --   is the same act's other half and adds no second measure and no second mapping.
  --   decisiveQuestion: Both forms are passage forms. 'On the Joint Resolution' is rule
  --   12's single PASSAGE_FORMS entry for a joint resolution in the Senate; 'On Passage'
  --   is the House's passage form. Admitted on form alone, so neither carries a
  --   decisiveWhy. The Senate's own motion-to-proceed roll on this resolution — 119/2 roll
  --   83, 51-49, 2026-04-15 — is refused on question form under rule 8 and recorded under
  --   declinedRollCalls.
  --   singleSubject: Read from the engrossed text (govinfo BILLS-119hjres140eh), which is
  --   one operative sentence in full: 'That Congress disapproves the rule submitted by the
  --   Bureau of Land Management of the Department of the Interior relating to Public Land
  --   Order No. 7917 for Withdrawal of Federal Lands; Cook, Lake, and Saint Louis
  --   Counties, MN (88 Fed. Reg. 6308 (January 31, 2023)), and such rule shall have no
  --   force or effect.' One subject, no reserve fund, no severable provision, no
  --   sense-of-Congress clause.
  --   notReserveFund: Correct. None of rule 31's three tells is present. The operative
  --   verb is 'disapproves'.
  --   proceduralInversion: No, in either chamber. Both questions are the resolution
  --   itself, so yeaBlocksMeasure() does not fire and a yea advances the disapproval in
  --   both rolls.
  --   nearUnanimity: No, in either chamber, and both were checked separately. Senate:
  --   50-49 with 1 not voting, losing side 49.495% of the pool. House: 214-208 with 9 not
  --   voting, losing side 49.289%. Both are among the most closely contested rolls in the
  --   corpus. Party totals from each document itself — Senate R 50-2, D 0-45, I 0-2; House
  --   R 213-1, D 1-207, and the House document's own totals-by-party block was checked
  --   against our own count of its member rows and agreed.
  --   twoFlankNays: Checked (rule 5 / rule 23) and NO, in both chambers. The nays hold one
  --   argument — that the withdrawal should stand. Three of them crossed over from the
  --   side that carried the resolution (two in the Senate, one in the House) and they are
  --   on that same side of the argument, not a second flank arguing the disapproval is too
  --   narrow. Headline key stands; no provision-level substitution. Same discipline as
  --   S.J.Res. 7: the check is on arguments, read from the floor debate, not on the
  --   tally's party columns.
  --   enactedTier: LAW. Enrolled, presented and approved 2026-04-27 as Public Law 119-85.
  --   Filed status 'enacted'. Under 5 U.S.C. 801(b) the disapproved order is now of no
  --   force or effect and a substantially similar one is barred.
  --   noticeNotRule: Recorded rather than smoothed. 88 Fed. Reg. 6308 is published in the
  --   Federal Register as a NOTICE, not as a final rule. Congress treated it as a rule for
  --   chapter 8 purposes and enactment settled the question; the mapping is filed on that
  --   basis and does not assert an independent view of what chapter 8 reaches.
  INSERT INTO vr_measure_issues (measure_id, issue_key, weight, is_primary, support_meaning, rationale, source_url) VALUES
    (m_119_h_j_res_140, 'lands_preserve', 90, true, 'yea_opposes',
      'The resolution nullifies Bureau of Land Management Public Land Order No. 7917, and both the resolution''s title and the order''s title name the same thing: “Withdrawal of Federal Lands”. The order states its own purpose in its Federal Register abstract — it withdraws “approximately 225,504 acres of National Forest System lands in Cook, Lake, and Saint Louis counties, Minnesota, from disposition under the United States mineral and geothermal leasing laws, for a period of 20 years, subject to valid existing rights, to protect and preserve the fragile and vital social and natural resources, ecological integrity, and wilderness values in the Rainy River Watershed, the Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness (BWCAW), the Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness Mining Protection Area (MPA), and the 1854 Ceded Territory of the Lake Superior Chippewa”. The instrument the disapproval acts on is therefore a conservation withdrawal, and a yea strips it. lands_preserve is ''Protect public lands & wild places for future generations'' and its keywords name ''wilderness'', ''national forest'', ''conservation'' and ''blm''. Primary at 90, the weight this key carries everywhere in the record — as a PRIMARY on H.J.Res. 78 and H.Amdt. 97, and as the mirror secondary on H.J.Res. 131. It is NOT filed the way H.J.Res. 131 was filed, and the reason is the test 131''s own rationale states: ''Not primary: the instrument acts on a leasing programme, and the conservation loss is the same act read from the other side.'' 131''s nullified instrument was the Coastal Plain Oil and Gas Leasing Program Record of Decision. This one''s is a withdrawal order for protection, so the two keys trade places and the resource-development gain is the same act read from the other side.',
      'https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/01/31/2023-01969/public-land-order-no-7917-for-withdrawal-of-federal-lands-cook-lake-and-saint-louis-counties-mn'),
    (m_119_h_j_res_140, 'lands_energy', 75, false, 'yea_supports',
      'The 225,504 acres the resolution returns to disposition are returned specifically ''under the United States mineral and geothermal leasing laws'', and the withdrawal the resolution strikes was imposed against ''the potential adverse effects of mineral and geothermal exploration and development''. lands_energy is ''Expand domestic energy, mining & resource development'' and its keywords name ''mining'', ''public land'', ''extraction'' and ''development'', so the axis reaches this directly. A yea reopens the acreage, which is yea_supports. This row is the exact mirror of H.J.Res. 131''s lands_preserve secondary, and it is a secondary for the mirrored reason: the instrument acts on the protection order, and the resource-development gain is the same act read from the other side. Weight 75 rather than 131''s 90 for its mirror row, and rather than the 40-60 the package-level lands_energy secondaries carry, because 75 is the weight H.J.Res. 131 argued for a secondary that acts DIRECTLY on the acreage rather than through a demand-side rule — the same reasoning, applied to the other key.',
      'https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/01/31/2023-01969/public-land-order-no-7917-for-withdrawal-of-federal-lands-cook-lake-and-saint-louis-counties-mn')
  ON CONFLICT (measure_id, issue_key) DO NOTHING;

END $$;

